  "usage": "Kafdeck CLI\n\nUsage:\n  kafdeck [global-options] system info\n  kafdeck [global-options] clusters list\n  kafdeck [global-options] clusters get \u003Ccluster-id\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] topics list \u003Ccluster-id\u003E [--search \u003Ctext\u003E] [--cursor \u003Copaque\u003E] [--limit \u003C1..200\u003E]\n  kafdeck [global-options] topics get \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Ctopic-name\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] consumer-groups list \u003Ccluster-id\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] consumer-groups get \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cgroup-id\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] consumer-groups lag \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cgroup-id\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] consumer-groups diagnostics \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cgroup-id\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] schemas subjects \u003Ccluster-id\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] schemas versions \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Csubject\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] schemas version \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Csubject\u003E \u003Cversion\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] schemas compatibility \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Csubject\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] schemas diff \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Csubject\u003E \u003Cleft-version\u003E \u003Cright-version\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] topics create-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Ctopic-name\u003E \u003Cpartitions\u003E \u003Creplication-factor\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] operations status \u003Coperation-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] operations confirm \u003Coperation-id\u003E \u003Cpreview-hash\u003E [--challenge \u003Ctyped-target\u003E]\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] operations execute \u003Coperation-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] topics delete-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Ctopic-name\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] topics alter-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Ctopic-name\u003E --config \u003Ckey=value\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] topics increase-partitions-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Ctopic-name\u003E \u003Ctarget-count\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] operations approval \u003Coperation-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] operations approve \u003Coperation-id\u003E \u003Cpreview-hash\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] operations reject \u003Coperation-id\u003E \u003Cpreview-hash\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E [global-options] operations cancel \u003Coperation-id\u003E \u003Cpreview-hash\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E catalog \u003Cteams|applications|topics\u003E \u003Ccluster-id\u003E [--cursor \u003Copaque\u003E] [--limit \u003C1..200\u003E]\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E catalog \u003Cget|history\u003E \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cteams|applications|topics\u003E \u003Crecord-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E catalog change-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cteams|applications|topics\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E catalog import-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E catalog plan \u003Coperation-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E catalog recover \u003Coperation-id\u003E --request-file \u003Cpreview-hash.json\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E policies \u003Cversions|state\u003E \u003Ccluster-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E policies version \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cversion-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E policies \u003Cvalidate|explain|dry-run\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E\n    Validation input is {\u0022clusterId\u0022:\u0022exact-scope\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:\u0022closed policy JSON\u0022}; validation never grants global read or execution rights.\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E policies \u003Cversion-preview|activate-preview\u003E \u003Ccluster-id\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E policies plan \u003Coperation-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E policies reconcile \u003Coperation-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E requests list \u003Ccluster-id\u003E [--cursor \u003Copaque\u003E] [--limit \u003C1..200\u003E]\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E requests \u003Cget|history\u003E \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Crequest-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E requests change-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E requests \u003Cplan|recover\u003E \u003Coperation-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E measurements list \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cfrom-utc\u003E \u003Cto-utc\u003E [resource-id]\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E attribution windows \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cfrom-utc\u003E \u003Cto-utc\u003E [resource-id]\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E dashboards show \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cfrom-utc\u003E \u003Cto-utc\u003E [resource-id]\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E rate-cards \u003Cversions|state\u003E \u003Ccluster-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E rate-cards \u003Cversion-preview|activate-preview\u003E \u003Ccluster-id\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E rate-cards \u003Cplan|recover\u003E \u003Coperation-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E records produce-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Ctopic-name\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E records produce-execute \u003Coperation-id\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E consumer-groups offsets-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cgroup-id\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E schemas register-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Csubject\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E connect create-preview \u003Ccluster-id\u003E \u003Cconnector\u003E --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E notifications recovery status\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E notifications recovery preview --request-file \u003Cclosed.json\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E notifications recovery approve \u003Coperation-id\u003E --request-file \u003Crevision-hash.json\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E notifications recovery apply \u003Coperation-id\u003E --request-file \u003Crevision-hash.json\u003E\n  kafdeck [global-options] capabilities mutations\n  kafdeck declarative validate --manifest-file \u003Cclosed.json|yaml\u003E --source \u003Cregistered-source\u003E --source-revision \u003Csha256\u003E --ownership-revision \u003Cnumber\u003E\n  kafdeck --service-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E declarative observe|drift|import|plan|reconcile --manifest-file \u003Cclosed.json|yaml\u003E --source \u003Cregistered-source\u003E --source-revision \u003Csha256\u003E --ownership-revision \u003Cnumber\u003E [--idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E] [--yes]\n  kafdeck --service-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E declarative apply \u003Cplan-id\u003E \u003Cplan-fingerprint\u003E\n  kafdeck --service-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E declarative recover \u003Cplan-id\u003E \u003Cplan-fingerprint\u003E\n  kafdeck --service-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E declarative show \u003Cplan-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --service-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E declarative capabilities\n  kafdeck --service-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E declarative source-show \u003Csource\u003E --resource \u003Cresource-id\u003E\n  kafdeck --service-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E declarative source-advance \u003Csource\u003E \u003Cexpected-generation\u003E \u003Cexpected-revision\u003E \u003Cexpected-hash\u003E --manifest-file \u003Cclosed.json|yaml\u003E\n  kafdeck --oidc-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E views v08-bearer-read-capabilities\n  kafdeck --service-profile \u003Cprofile\u003E views \u003Cexact-versioned-view-name\u003E \u003Cpath-identities...\u003E [--request-file \u003Cclosed-query-or-body.json\u003E]\n  kafdeck --help\n\nGlobal options:\n  --url \u003Cbase-url\u003E\n  --token-file \u003Cpath\u003E\n  --oidc-profile \u003Cpublic-profile.json\u003E  Sign in using browser PKCE; memory-only bearer for this command.\n  --service-profile \u003Cpublic-profile.json\u003E  Sign in with a referenced RSA private key; memory-only service bearer.\n  --output json\n  --idempotency-key \u003Ckey\u003E  Required for a named mutation preview; recovery has its own revision/hash CAS.\n  --request-file \u003Cpath\u003E   Bounded closed payload for a named family command; no generic JSON or provider route.\n  --challenge \u003Ctarget\u003E    Admitted only for operation confirmation.\n  --config \u003Ckey=value\u003E   Repeat unique allowed keys for topic create/alter preview.\n  --reset-config \u003Ckey\u003E   Reset a unique allowed topic key; alter preview only.\n\nEnvironment:\n  KAFDECK_URL\n  KAFDECK_ACCESS_TOKEN\n\nSecurity:\n  Access tokens are intentionally not accepted as command-line arguments.\n  Use KAFDECK_ACCESS_TOKEN or --token-file.\n  The CLI exposes only typed governed API routes; there is no arbitrary HTTP path passthrough.\n  Governed commands require non-browser OIDC and explicit backend family admission.\n  Approval and recovery commands require eligible human identities. Missing runtime families remain unavailable.",
